course: dictionary
lesson: 12633
title: Disorient
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To disorient someone is to make them confused about where they are or which way to go, or unable to think clearly. «The thick fog disoriented the hikers, and they could not tell which way the path led.» The clue is «could not tell which way», so disoriented means lost and confused.
explain: The word has two parts. Dis- often means "not" or "take away", and orient is about direction and finding your way. So to disorient someone is to take away their sense of direction. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "confused about which way to go" still makes sense.
explain: Words can also describe feelings and experiences. «The spinning ride left Mia feeling disoriented.» «It was a disorienting experience.» Disoriented describes the person who feels confused, and disorienting describes the thing that causes it.
fact: Disorient means to make someone confused about where they are or which way to go.
fact: Disorient can also mean to make someone confused and unable to think clearly.
fact: Disorient is a verb: disorients, disoriented, disorienting.
fact: «Disoriented» describes someone who feels confused: «She felt disoriented after the bump on her head.»
fact: In science, some animals become disoriented by bright city lights, so they lose their way.
exercise: «The thick fog disoriented the hikers.» What does disoriented mean here? | Full of sunshine | Warm and cosy | Very fast and excited | *Confused about which way to go
exercise: Some birds become disoriented by bright city lights. What does this suggest? | They fly faster and get home sooner | They sing louder than before | They sleep in the sun | *They become confused and lose their way
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to disorient? | measure | cheer up | *confuse | polish
test: «The spinning ride was a disorienting experience.» What kind of experience was it? | One that you had at school | *One that left you confused and dizzy | One that made you laugh with friends | One that was over in a second
test: Which sentence uses disoriented correctly? | Sam felt disoriented and ate a big lunch. | The disoriented sun rose in the east. | The river was disoriented and cold. | *After the bang on his head, Sam felt disoriented and could not remember the way home.
exam: «Mum said the bright lights made her feel disoriented in the city.» What does disoriented mean? | Quick and clever | *Confused and unsure where you are | Happy and relaxed | Hungry
